[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Enterprise RBAC, Private Network Agents, and Performance Testing in Postman"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"This technical tutorial explores advanced enterprise features in Postman, focusing on Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) security, communicating with internal services via Private Network Agents, and executing enterprise-scale performance tests."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Configuring Enterprise RBAC"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Postman Enterprise allows organizations to enforce security through granular Role-Based Access Control. Administrators can assign custom roles to restrict access to production environments, sensitive workspaces, and collection variables."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Partner Manager / Administrator: Full control over team management, SCIM provisioning, and global workspace settings."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Editor: Can modify collections, run tests, and manage environment variables within assigned workspaces."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Viewer: Read-only access to collections and documentation, preventing accidental modifications to production APIs."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Setting Up Private Network Agents"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"When testing internal microservices that reside behind a corporate firewall or within a VPC, Postman allows you to route requests securely through a Private Network Agent without exposing your endpoints to the public internet."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"docker run -e POSTMAN_API_KEY="PMAK-your-api-key" -e AGENT_NAME="Corp-Internal-Agent" postman/private-network-agent"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once the agent is active, navigate to your Postman Desktop app or Web client, select the environment, and configure the request to use your newly registered Private Network Agent under Request Settings."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Executing Enterprise Performance Tests"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Postman enables you to run load tests directly from your collections to evaluate API resilience under high traffic loads. You can configure virtual users (VUs), ramp-up periods, and load distribution strategies."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"import { htmlReport } from "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/benc-uk/k6-reporter/main/dist/bundle.js";
export function handleSummary(data) {
  return { "summary.html": htmlReport(data) };
}"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"To execute a performance test in Postman, open any collection, click the three dots, select 'Run collection', and switch to the Performance tab. Define your virtual users and duration, then analyze real-time metrics such as latency, throughput, and error rates."}]
